module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.CohenRing
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Torsion.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.KrullDimension.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Defs

/-!
# Residue-preserving parameter maps for complete local domains

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma Tag 032D, the parameter construction in Cases I and II.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-complete-local-domain-residue-parameter-map)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u
set_option autoImplicit false

namespace IsLocalRing

/-- The parameter construction gives a power-series algebra of the same dimension, with
Hausdorff target, finite reduction, and a surjective map to the target residue field.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma Tag 032D, Cases I and II before the application of
Lemma Tag 031D. (blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-complete-local-domain-residue-parameter-map)

Proof:
1. Choose a coefficient subring by the Cohen structure theorem, Tag 032A(1). Because R is
   a domain, this coefficient subring is either a field or a Cohen ring: in equal
   characteristic its maximal ideal is zero; in mixed characteristic it is generated by
   the nonzero residue characteristic p, and completeness makes it a discrete valuation ring.
2. In the field case choose dim R parameters generating an ideal of definition I. In the
   Cohen case p is a nonzerodivisor, so dim(R/pR) + 1 = dim R. Choose dim(R/pR) parameters
   modulo p and lift them to R; together with p they generate an ideal of definition I.
   In either case some power of the maximal ideal is contained in I, and I lies in it.
3. Change-ideal completeness (Tag 0319) makes R I-adically complete. Evaluate formal power
   series at these parameters, using the coefficient inclusion, to define the algebra
   structure on R. The source maximal ideal is generated by the variables, and also p
   in the Cohen case, so its extension to R is I. Its powers acting on R are I^k.
4. The power-series dimension calculation (Tag 032C) gives dimension n in the field case
   and n+1 in the Cohen case. The choice in step 2 gives equality with dim R.
5. Since R is I-adically complete, the intersection of I^k is zero. The equality in step 3
   therefore gives Hausdorffness for the source maximal ideal acting on R.
6. R/I is Artinian local because I is an ideal of definition in a Noetherian local ring.
   Its residue field is that of R, and hence that of the coefficient ring and the source.
   The source residue field acts on R/I because its maximal ideal maps into I. The quotient
   of R/I by its Jacobson radical is cyclic over this field. The finite-length theorem
   for Artinian local rings (Tag 00JB) therefore makes R/I finite over the source residue
   field; this also applies in mixed characteristic since p acts by zero on R/I.
   The module quotient by the source maximal ideal acting
   on R identifies with R/I, which proves the final clause.

7. Every residue class of R has a representative in the coefficient subring, by the
   coefficient-ring residue isomorphism. The parameter evaluation sends each constant
   series to that representative. Thus the composite of evaluation with R → R/m is
   surjective. This is a property of the constructed map, not of an arbitrary finite
   regular subring.

This only constructs the parameter map and proves its reduction properties. Its finiteness
and injectivity are subsequent steps of Tag 032D, not assumptions of this assertion. -/
theorem complete_local_domain_residue_parameter_map
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R] :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (Λ : Type u) (_ : CommRing Λ),
      ∃ (_ : IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
        (_ : Algebra (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) R),
        (IsField Λ ∨ ∃ p : ℕ, IsCohenRing p Λ) ∧
        ringKrullDim (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) = ringKrullDim R ∧
        IsHausdorff (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) R ∧
        Module.Finite
          (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ ⧸ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
          (R ⧸ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) • ⊤ :
            Submodule (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) R)) ∧
        Function.Surjective ((residue R).comp
          (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) R)) := by sorry

end IsLocalRing
